# CTAN: Comprehensive TeX Archive Network

## Overview
[CTAN](https://ctan.org/): The Comprehensive TeX Archive Network is a central repository for TeX-related software, documentation, and resources. It serves as a central repository of TeX packages for users and developers in the TeX community.

## Browsing and Searching
[Browse](https://ctan.org/tex-archive): A method to explore the various packages and resources available on CTAN.

[Packages](https://ctan.org/pkg): A comprehensive list of all packages hosted on CTAN, categorized for easy access.

[Topics](https://ctan.org/topics): A categorized listing of topics covered by the packages available on CTAN.

[Contributors](https://ctan.org/author): A comprehensive list of all contributors and their packages on CTAN.

[Search](https://ctan.org/search): A basic search functionality to find specific packages or documentation within the CTAN archive.

[Extended search](https://ctan.org/search?ext=new): An advanced search option that allows users to refine their queries for more precise results.

[File search](https://ctan.org/search?ext=false&FILES=on): A specialized search tool for locating specific files within the CTAN repository.

## Announcements
[Announcements](https://ctan.org/ctan-ann): A section dedicated to news and updates regarding CTAN, including new package releases and important changes.

## Background and Community
[CTAN Background](https://ctan.org/ctan): Provides historical context and information about the development and purpose of CTAN.

[TeX user groups](https://ctan.org/lugs): A list of user groups dedicated to TeX, offering support and resources for users in various regions.

## Getting Started
[Starting out with TeX...](https://ctan.org/starter): A guide for beginners to help them understand the basics of TeX and how to get started with typesetting documents.

## Technical Resources
[Licenses](https://ctan.org/license): Information on the licensing of packages and software available on CTAN, ensuring users understand their rights and responsibilities.

## Uploading Packages
[Upload](https://ctan.org/upload): Instructions for contributors on how to submit new packages or updates to existing ones.

[Upload basics](https://ctan.org/help/upload-pkg): A brief overview of the requirements and processes involved in uploading content to CTAN.

[Upload addendum](https://ctan.org/file/help/ctan/CTAN-upload-addendum): Additional information and guidelines for contributors regarding the upload process.

## Additional Resources
[Contact](https://ctan.org/contact): Details on how to get in touch with the CTAN team for inquiries or support.

[Feedback](mailto:webmaster@ctan.org?subject=Feedback%20for%20/?lang=en): A section for users to provide feedback on their experiences with CTAN.

[Guest Book](https://ctan.org/guestbook): A place for visitors to leave comments and messages for the CTAN community.

[Privacy](https://ctan.org/privacy): Information regarding the privacy policies and practices of CTAN.

[Sitemap](https://ctan.org/sitemap): A structured overview of the CTAN website, helping users navigate the available resources.

[Credits](https://ctan.org/credits): Acknowledgments of contributors and supporters of the CTAN project.

## Technical Support
[Help](https://ctan.org/help): A resource for users seeking assistance with using CTAN or troubleshooting issues.

[Settings](https://ctan.org/user/settings): User-specific settings for managing preferences and account details.

## Content Delivery Network
[CDN Hosts](https://www.ctan.org/mirrors): A comprehensive list of the mirror hosts all over the world.
 
[Becoming A CTAN Mirror](https://ctan.org/mirrors/register): Guidelines for organizations interested in becoming a mirror site for CTAN, helping to distribute the load and improve access.

## Related Projects
[TeX Live](https://ctan.org/pkg/texlive): A comprehensive TeX distribution that includes a wide range of TeX-related software.

[MacTeX](https://ctan.org/pkg/mactex): A TeX distribution specifically designed for macOS users.

[TeX Users Group (TUG)](http://tug.org/): An organization that supports the TeX community through resources, conferences, and publications.

[Deutschsprachige Anwendervereinigung TeX e.V. (DANTE)](http://www.dante.de/): A German-speaking user group dedicated to promoting TeX and its applications.
